# XCU ipcrm
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The whole utility is XSI-shaded. No POSIX utility creates a message queue,
# semaphore set or shared memory segment for ipcrm to remove, so the tests
# cover the no-option form and the error for identifiers and keys that no
# facility has (values chosen far above and away from usual ones).

assertion  XCU.ipcrm.001
anchor     utilities/ipcrm.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/ipcrm.html#EXIT STATUS
class      conditional
when       XSI
says       ipcrm without options removes nothing and exits with status zero,
           writing nothing to standard output.
test       t/001-no-options.sh

assertion  XCU.ipcrm.002
anchor     utilities/ipcrm.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/ipcrm.html#EXIT STATUS
class      conditional
when       XSI
says       Removing a message queue, semaphore set or shared memory segment
           by an identifier or a key that no facility has (-q, -s, -m, -Q,
           -S, -M) cannot be done: ipcrm exits with a status above zero.
test       t/002-no-such-facility.sh

assertion  XCU.ipcrm.003
anchor     utilities/ipcrm.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/ipcrm.html#DESCRIPTION
class      untestable
when       XSI
says       ipcrm removes the facility named by -q, -m or -s (identifier) or
           -Q, -M or -S (key), a shared memory segment being destroyed after
           the last detach, and only a process with appropriate privileges may
           remove a facility it does not own.
reason     No POSIX utility creates one of these facilities to remove, and
           ownership by another user cannot be arranged portably.
